# Registry of models this box can launch agents against.
#
# Copy it and fill in real values:
#     cp models.conf.example models.conf
#
# models.conf is NOT versioned: it holds your tailnet name and the 100.x
# addresses of your nodes. This file is the reference for the shape.
#
# The servers themselves are not part of this project. They are llama.cpp
# instances serving an OpenAI-compatible API; the setup used here is
# llamacpp-compose:
#
#     https://github.com/nicoRomeroCuruchet/llamacpp-compose
#
# Anything that answers /health and /v1/models in that format works.
#
# Format — three whitespace-separated fields, in this order:
#
#     <alias>   <base_url>   <ip>
#
#   alias     The llama-server --alias serving that model. It must match what
#             /v1/models returns EXACTLY: OMP receives it as `llama.cpp/<alias>`.
#             It is also the agent's name in herdr and the pane title.
#   base_url  Full URL with scheme, no trailing slash (an extra slash produces
#             //v1/chat/completions and a 404 that looks like something else).
#   ip        The node's 100.x tailnet address. NOT optional: the container's
#             resolver does not know MagicDNS, so the name would not resolve
#             inside it. run.sh builds one --add-host per line. TLS still
#             validates, because the `tailscale serve` certificate is for that
#             same name. Get it from `tailscale status`.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# The FIRST model listed is what `spawn-model` uses with no arguments.

qwen38-27b   https://YOUR-NODE.YOUR-TAILNET.ts.net    100.x.y.z
ornith-35b   https://OTHER-NODE.YOUR-TAILNET.ts.net   100.x.y.z
